(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-26"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-26","label":"2026 年 8 月 26 日","date":"2026-08-26","range":"","theme":"商业","themes":["商业"],"sources":["The Guardian"],"title":"Will AI destroy film industry or usher in","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":11,"vocab":32,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"8.26 精读.pdf","headline":{"title":"Will AI destroy film industry or usher in","titleZh":"","source":"The Guardian","series":"考研那些事儿之商业系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Near the colonnaded entrance to Sony Pictures’ Culver City film studio, a tech-powered rival has sprung up this summer. The artists at Promise, a new studio feeding off the potential of AI, can see the lots where Singin’ in the Rain and Men in Black were shot, but no longer do they need to get beyond the studio’s high walls to make their visions come true.","zh":"今年夏天，在索尼影业卡尔弗城制片的柱廊入口附近，一家科技驱动的竞争对手悄然崛起。Promise是一家以借助人工智能（AI）创作的新锐工作室，其艺术家们在工作室就可以望见索尼《雨中曲》和《黑衣人》的拍摄场地，但如今他们已无需越过制片厂的高墙，就能将自己的构想变为现实。"},{"index":2,"en":"From far more modest premises, they are making movies with rapidly accelerating AI models that create backgrounds, special effects and even “synthetic performers” – using US models but also driven by market-leading Chinese AI. Backed by Google, Silicon Valley venture capitalists and Disney, Promise is one of a rising number of AI film studios in Hollywood.","zh":"尽管与索尼相比，他们的办公场所要小得多，他们正利用飞速迭代的AI模型制作电影——这些模型能够生成背景、特效，甚至“合成演员”，它们既采用美国模型，也依托中国市场领先的AI技术。在谷歌、硅谷风险投资家和迪士尼的支持下，Promise已成为好莱坞日益增多的AI电影工作室之一。"},{"index":3,"en":"It is a controversial trend. Leading directors including Christopher Nolan and Guillermo del Toro have criticised generative technology, actors and writers are fearing for their jobs, and the Democrat congresswoman Laura Friedman, who represents Hollywood’s actors, writers and directors, warned: “We can’t wait until we see tens of thousands of American workers displaced.”","zh":"这一趋势颇具争议。包括克里斯托弗·诺兰和吉尔莫·德尔·托罗在内的顶尖导演曾批评生成式技术，演员和编剧们也担心自己的饭碗不保。代表好莱坞演员、编剧和导演的民主党众议员劳拉·弗里德曼警告道：“我们不能等到看着数万名美国工人失业后，才采取行动。”"},{"index":4,"en":"But the excitement and energy about AI was palpable this week at Promise’s new base, when a human actor, Tori Thomas, waited for her call amid rows of computers on the studio’s AI-enabled horror film, Touch Grass, with a budget in the low millions of dollars.","zh":"但本周在Promise的新基地，人们对人工智能的热情与活力显而易见。当时，真人演员托里·托马斯正置身于工作室中一排排电脑之间，等待拍摄指令，她正在参与一部由人工智能辅助制作的恐怖电影《TouchGrass》，该片的预算在数百万美元左右。"},{"index":5,"en":"The sound stage was a corner of the office hung with white sheets. A small camera followed Thomas as she scrambled in a chase scene, then the AI superimposed her movement in real-time on to a field of swaying grass generated by a new Chinese AI model, Seedance 2.5, which looks as if it will slash production times. Whole scenes – actor and backdrop – were visible on the director’s handheld monitor as if they were filming in real locations. With a glance at the screen, Thomas could immediately see the backdrop she was acting with.","zh":"摄影棚就在公室的一个角落，四周挂着白色幕布。当托里·托马斯在追逐场景中四处奔跑时，一台小型摄像机跟拍着她，随后人工智能将她的动作实时叠加到由中国新型AI模型“Seedance2.5”生成的随风摇曳的草地上——该模型有望将大幅缩短制作周期。整个场景——包括演员和背景——都清晰地呈现在导演手持的监视器上，仿佛是在实景进行的拍摄。托马斯只需瞥一眼屏幕，就能立即看到自己正在与之互动的背景。"},{"index":6,"en":"Promise is not alone in embracing the technology, which Netflix last week said it had used in 300 of its 1,000 titles in 2026. Imagine, the 41-year-old studio run by Brian Grazer and Ron Howard, the director of The Da Vinci Code and A Beautiful Mind, now has an AI studio, Obsidian, operating from space in its Beverly Hills HQ. Imagine has partnered with Obsidian to make The Code, an AI-enabled, Howard-directed animated feature based on drawings made in Vietnamese captivity by US prisoners of war.","zh":"Promise并非唯一一家采用这项技术的公司。Netflix上周表示，在2026年的1000部作品中，已有300部采用了该技术。由布莱恩·格雷泽和曾执导《达芬奇密码》《美丽心灵》的罗恩·霍华德共同运营的制片公司Imagine，已有41年历史，如今也在其比佛利山庄总部内设立了名为“黑曜石”（Obsidian）的AI工作室。Imagine已与黑曜石合作制作《密码》（TheCode）——这是一部由霍华德执导、基于美国战俘在越南被俘期间所绘制的手稿改编的AI动画长片。"},{"index":7,"en":"Brad Pitt this week said that, although there was a lot of resistance, “AI is going to be the very thing that, if used as a tool, is going to help these mid-budget films, $40m to $90m-budgeted films, get made.” That chimed with predictions from a new wave of AI native film-makers, such as Kavan “the Kid” Cardoza, 37, who has set up the Phantom X studio. He predicted a creative renaissance circumventing the studio giants not seen in more than 30 years.","zh":"布拉德·皮特本周表示，尽管存在诸多阻力，“但如果将人工智能作为工具加以利用，它将大大助力这些中等预算的电影（即预算在4000万至9000万美元之间）完成制作。”这一观点与新一代“原生AI”电影制作人的预测不谋而合，例如37岁的卡万·“小鬼”·卡多扎（Kavan“theKid”Cardoza），他创立了PhantomX工作室。他预测，一场绕过大型制片厂的创意复兴即将到来，而这是此前30多年来未曾见过的。"},{"index":8,"en":"The Promise shoot involved veteran film-makers including Joel Hynek, an Oscar-winner who worked on the manual special effects for Arnold Schwarzenegger’s 1987 action-horror film Predator. “When we went from optical to digital film, we thought we’d gone to heaven,” he told the Guardian.","zh":"Promise的拍摄团队汇聚了多位资深电影人，例如奥斯卡奖得主乔尔·海涅克——他曾参与阿诺德·施瓦辛格1987年动作恐怖片《铁血战士》的手工特效制作。“当我们从光学胶片转向数字电影时，我们仿佛置身天堂，”他告诉《卫报》。"},{"index":9,"en":"Others, such as Nolan, voice concern. “I’ve never seen a technology advancing so rapidly, so completely rejected by the public,” the director of The Odyssey has said. “Everybody’s suspicion of it is so extreme, particularly young people.”","zh":"与此同时，诺兰等人则表达了担忧。这位《奥德赛》的导演曾表示：“我从未见过一项技术发展如此迅速，却又被公众如此排斥。大家对它的戒心非常强烈，尤其是年轻人。”"},{"index":10,"en":"There has been opposition to an AI resurrection of the late actor Val Kilmer to star in a new feature and the emergence of the AI “actor” Tilly Norwood, with the actor Emily Blunt pleading: “Please stop taking away our human connection.”","zh":"针对利用人工智能“复活”已故演员瓦尔·基尔默出演新片，以及人工智能“演员”蒂莉·诺伍德的出现，外界出现了反对声浪。演员艾米丽·布朗特恳求道：“请别再剥夺我们的人际联结。”"},{"index":11,"en":"But the new AI studios are undeterred. Dave Clark, director of Promise’s Touch Grass said that with “great dialogue and backstory” AI-generated characters can become interesting and believable. The actors’ union SAG-Aftra will no doubt beg to differ, but Cardoza predicted “next year [AI actors will] be just as good as real actors”. George Strompolos, co-founder and chief executive of Promise, estimated hybrid AI films – human actors alongside AI technology – will prove 20% to 50% cheaper than conventional production. That could free film-makers from requiring major studio investment.","zh":"但新兴的AI制片公司并未因此却步。Promise旗下《TouchGrass》的导演戴夫·克拉克表示，只要拥有“精彩的台词和背景故事”，AI生成的角色就能变得生动有趣且令人信服。演员工会SAG-AFTRA无疑会持不同意见，但卡多扎预测：“明年，AI演员的表现将与真人演员一样出色。”Promise公司的联合创始人兼首席执行官乔治·斯特罗姆波洛斯估计，混合型AI电影——即真人演员与AI技术并用的模式——制作成本将比传统制作低20%至50%。电影制作人或可以由此摆脱对大型制片厂投资的依赖。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"usher /ˈʌʃə(r)/ in v. (formal) to be the beginning of sth new","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"or to make sth new begin 开创；开始；开启","example":"The change of management ushered in fresh ideas and","exampleZh":"policies.更换领导班子带来了新思想和新政策。","tags":[]},{"term":"colonnaded a. /ˌkɒləˈneɪdɪd/ 有柱列的","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"feed off","head":"n. (of an animal 动物) to eat sth 以…为食","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"Butterflies feed on the flowers of garden plants. 蝴蝶以园林","exampleZh":"中草木的花为食。","tags":[]},{"term":"spring up","head":"v. to appear or develop quickly and/or suddenly","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"迅速出现；突然兴起【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"lot","head":"n. an area of land used for a particular purpose（作某种","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"用途的）一块地，场地【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"a parking lot 停车场 今年夏天，在索尼影业卡尔弗城制片的柱廊入口附近，一 家科技驱动的竞争对手悄然崛起。Promise是一家以借助人工 智能（AI）创作的新锐工作室，其艺术家们在工作室就可以望 见索尼《雨中曲》和《黑衣人》的拍摄场地，但如今他们已无 需越过制片厂的高墙，就能将自己的构想变为现实。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"accelerate","head":"v. to happen or to make sth happen faster or","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"earlierthanexpected（使）加速，加快【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Inflation continues to accelerate. 通货膨胀不断加速。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"synthetic a. artificial; made by combining chemical","head":"","definition":"substances rather than being produced naturally by plants","gloss":"oranimals人造的；（人工）合成的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"SYN man-made","exampleZh":"synthetic drugs/fabrics 合成药物╱织物 尽管与索尼相比，他们的办公场所要小得多，他们正利用 飞速迭代的AI模型制作电影——这些模型能够生成背景、特效， 甚至“合成演员”，它们既采用美国模型，也依托中国市场领 先的AI技术。在谷歌、硅谷风险投资家和迪士尼的支持下， Promise已成为好莱坞日益增多的AI电影工作室之一。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"controversial a. /ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl/ causing a lot of angry public","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"discussionanddisagreement引起争论的；有争议的【️【️考研大","exampleZh":"纲词汇】 a highly controversial topic 颇有争议的话题","tags":[]},{"term":"displaced a. If a person or group of people is displaced,","head":"","definition":"they are forced to move away from the area where they live.","gloss":"使背井离乡【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"More than 600,000 people were displaced by the","exampleZh":"tsunami.超过60万人被海啸搞得背井离乡。 这一趋势颇具争议。包括克里斯托弗·诺兰和吉尔莫·德尔· 托罗在内的顶尖导演曾批评生成式技术，演员和编剧们也担心 自己的饭碗不保。代表好莱坞演员、编剧和导演的民主党众议 员劳拉·弗里德曼警告道：“我们不能等到看着数万名美国工人 失业后，才采取行动。”","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"palpable a. /ˈpælpəbəl/ You describe something as","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"palpable when it is obvious or intense and easily noticed. 可","exampleZh":"感知的;明显的 The tension between Amy and Jim is palpable. 埃米和吉姆之 间的紧张关系是显而易见的。","tags":[]},{"term":"enable","head":"v. If someone or something enables you to do a","definition":"","gloss":"particular thing, they give you the opportunity to do it. 使","example":"The new test should enable doctors to detect the disease","exampleZh":"能够【️【️考研大纲词汇】 early.新的检验使医生能在早期发现该种疾病。 但本周在Promise的新基地，人们对人工智能的热情与活 力显而易见。当时，真人演员托里·托马斯正置身于工作室中一 排排电脑之间，等待拍摄指令，她正在参与一部由人工智能辅 助制作的恐怖电影《TouchGrass》，该片的预算在数百万美元 左右。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"scramble","head":"v. If you scramble over rocks or up a hill, you","definition":"move quickly over them or up it using your hands to help","gloss":"you.攀爬【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"Tourists were scrambling over the rocks looking for the","exampleZh":"perfectcameraangle.旅行者们爬上岩石，寻找最完美的拍摄 角度。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"superimpose","head":"v. If one image is superimposed on another,","definition":"it is put on top of it so that you can see the second image","gloss":"through it. 叠加","example":"The image of a seemingly tiny dancer was superimposed on","exampleZh":"theimageofthetable.一个看似很小的舞蹈者的影像被叠加在 了那张桌子的影像上。","tags":[]},{"term":"slash","head":"v. [often passive] (often used in newspapers 常用于报","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"章) to reduce sth by a large amount 大幅度削减；大大降低","exampleZh":"toslashcosts/prices/fares,etc.大幅度降低成本、价格、车费 等","tags":[]},{"term":"handheld a. A handheld device such as a camera or a","head":"","definition":"computer is small and light enough to be used while you","gloss":"","example":"areholdingit.手持式的;掌上的","exampleZh":"...a handheld electric mixer. …一个手持式电动搅拌器 摄影棚就在公室的一个角落，四周挂着白色幕布。当托里· 托马斯在追逐场景中四处奔跑时，一台小型摄像机跟拍着她， 随后人工智能将她的动作实时叠加到由中国新型AI模型 “Seedance2.5”生成的随风摇曳的草地上——该模型有望将 大幅缩短制作周期。整个场景——包括演员和背景——都清晰 地呈现在导演手持的监视器上，仿佛是在实景进行的拍摄。托 马斯只需瞥一眼屏幕，就能立即看到自己正在与之互动的背景。","tags":[]},{"term":"embrace","head":"v. If you embrace a change, political system, or","definition":"idea, you accept it and start supporting it or believing in it.","gloss":"","example":"欣然接受;信奉【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"He embraces the new information age. 他欢迎新的信息时代。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"animated a. An animated film is one in which puppets or","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"drawings appear to move. 动画的","example":"Disney has returned to what it does best: making full-length","exampleZh":"animatedfeaturefilms.迪斯尼电影公司回到他们最拿手的事 情：制作长篇动画故事片。","tags":[]},{"term":"captivity","head":"n. /kæpˈtɪvəti/ [U] the state of being kept as a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"prisoner or in a confined space 监禁；关押；困住","exampleZh":"He was held in captivity for three years. 他被监禁了三年。 Promise并非唯一一家采用这项技术的公司。Netflix上周 表示，在2026年的1000部作品中，已有300部采用了该技 术。由布莱恩·格雷泽和曾执导《达芬奇密码》《美丽心灵》的 罗恩·霍华德共同运营的制片公司Imagine，已有41年历史， 如今也在其比佛利山庄总部内设立了名为“黑曜石” （Obsidian）的AI工作室。Imagine已与黑曜石合作制作《密 码》（TheCode）——这是一部由霍华德执导、基于美国战俘 在越南被俘期间所绘制的手稿改编的AI动画长片。","tags":[]},{"term":"chime (in) with sth phrase(of plans, ideas, etc.计划、主意","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"等) to agree with sth; to be similar to sth 与…相一致（或相","exampleZh":"似） His opinions chimed in with the mood of the nation. 他的主 张与国民的心态相吻合。","tags":[]},{"term":"renaissance","head":"n. a situation when there is new interest in a","definition":"particular subject, form of art, etc. after a period when it was","gloss":"notverypopular（某一学科或艺术形式等衰落后的）复兴【️【️考","example":"SYN revival","exampleZh":"研大纲词汇】 to experience a renaissance 经历复兴","tags":[]},{"term":"circumvent","head":"v. /ˌsɜːkəmˈvent/ (formal) to find a way of","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"avoiding a difficulty or a rule 设法回避；规避","exampleZh":"They found a way of circumventing the law. 他们找到了规避 法律的途径。 布拉德·皮特本周表示，尽管存在诸多阻力，“但如果将人 工智能作为工具加以利用，它将大大助力这些中等预算的电影 （即预算在4000万至9000万美元之间）完成制作。”这一 观点与新一代“原生AI”电影制作人的预测不谋而合，例如37 岁的卡万·“小鬼”·卡多扎（Kavan“theKid”Cardoza），他 创立了PhantomX工作室。他预测，一场绕过大型制片厂的创 意复兴即将到来，而这是此前30多年来未曾见过的。","tags":[]},{"term":"veteran a. /ˈvetərən/ a person who has a lot of experience","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"inaparticularareaoractivity经验丰富的人；老手【️【️考研大纲","exampleZh":"词汇】 the veteran British actor, Sir Richard Attenborough 英国资深 演员理查德·阿滕伯勒爵士","tags":[]},{"term":"manual a. /ˈmænjuəl/ (of work, etc.工作等) involving using","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"thehandsorphysicalstrength用手的；手工的；体力的【️【️考","exampleZh":"研大纲词汇】 manuallabour/jobs/skills体力劳动╱活儿；手工技巧 Promise的拍摄团队汇聚了多位资深电影人，例如奥斯卡 奖得主乔尔·海涅克——他曾参与阿诺德·施瓦辛格1987年动作 恐怖片《铁血战士》的手工特效制作。“当我们从光学胶片转 向数字电影时，我们仿佛置身天堂，”他告诉《卫报》。","tags":[]},{"term":"suspicion","head":"n. /səˈspɪʃn/ ~ (that...) a feeling that sb has done","definition":"sth wrong, illegal or dishonest, even though you have no","gloss":"","example":"proof怀疑；嫌疑【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"They drove away slowly to avoid arousing suspicion. 他们缓 缓驾车离去，以免引起怀疑。 与此同时，诺兰等人则表达了担忧。这位《奥德赛》的导 演曾表示：“我从未见过一项技术发展如此迅速，却又被公众 如此排斥。大家对它的戒心非常强烈，尤其是年轻人。”","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"opposition","head":"n. /ˌɒpəˈzɪʃn/ [U] ~ (to sb/sth) the act of","definition":"strongly disagreeing with sb/sth, especially with the aim of","gloss":"","example":"preventingsthfromhappening（强烈的）反对，反抗，对抗","exampleZh":"Delegates expressed strong opposition to the plans. 代表强 烈反对这些计划。","tags":[]},{"term":"late a. [only before noun] (of a person 人) no longer alive 已","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"故的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"her late husband 她已故的丈夫","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"emergence","head":"n. /ɪˈmɜːdʒəns/ The emergence of something is","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"the process or event of its coming into existence. 兴起","exampleZh":"...the emergence of new democracies in Latin America. …拉 丁美洲新民主国家的兴起。 针对利用人工智能“复活”已故演员瓦尔·基尔默出演新片， 以及人工智能“演员”蒂莉·诺伍德的出现，外界出现了反对声 浪。演员艾米丽·布朗特恳求道：“请别再剥夺我们的人际联 结。”","tags":[]},{"term":"undeterred a. /ˌʌndɪˈtɜːd/ if sb is undeterred by sth, they","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"do not allow it to stop them from doing sth 顽强的；坚毅的；","exampleZh":"不屈不挠的","tags":[]},{"term":"backstory","head":"n. /ˈbækstɔːri/ the things that are supposed to","definition":"have happened before the events in a film/movie, novel, etc.","gloss":"","example":"（电影、小说等的）幕后故事，故事背景","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"beg to differ phraseused to say politely that you do not","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"agree with sth that has just been said 很抱歉，我不敢苟同","exampleZh":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hybrid a. of mixed character, composed of mixed parts 混","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"合的；混合而成的","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"alongside","head":"prep. together with or at the same time as sth/sb","definition":"","gloss":"与…一起；与…同时【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"Traditional beliefs still flourish alongside a modern urban 17 August 2026 | The Guardian","exampleZh":"lifestyle.现代城市生活方式盛行的同时，传统信念仍然大行其道。 但新兴的AI制片公司并未因此却步。Promise旗下 《TouchGrass》的导演戴夫·克拉克表示，只要拥有“精彩的 台词和背景故事”，AI生成的角色就能变得生动有趣且令人信 服。演员工会SAG-AFTRA无疑会持不同意见，但卡多扎预测： “明年，AI演员的表现将与真人演员一样出色。”Promise公 司的联合创始人兼首席执行官乔治·斯特罗姆波洛斯估计，混合 型AI电影——即真人演员与AI技术并用的模式——制作成本 将比传统制作低20%至50%。电影制作人或可以由此摆脱对大 型制片厂投资的依赖。 群公告学习流程精读，","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.26 检验题__阅读理解.docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1 and 2, Promise is described as a rival to traditional studios because it _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rents sound stages inside Sony Pictures' Culver City lot"},{"key":"B","text":"relies solely on American AI models to produce synthetic performers"},{"key":"C","text":"makes films outside the old studio system by using AI to create backgrounds, effects and digital performers"},{"key":"D","text":"has completely replaced human actors with AI-generated characters"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·公司特征识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-2","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：A tech-powered rival has sprung up this summer...no longer do they need to get beyond the studio’s high walls to make their visions come true.","- 原文（Para.2）：They are making movies with rapidly accelerating AI models that create backgrounds, special effects and even “synthetic performers”...","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。Promise 的办公位置能看到 Sony 片场，但原文没有说它租用 Sony 的摄影棚。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文明确说它 using US models but also driven by market-leading Chinese AI，并不是 solely American models。","- 选项C（正确）：Para.1 强调它不再需要进入传统制片厂高墙，Para.2 说明其用 AI 生成背景、特效甚至 synthetic performers。C 项完整概括其竞争性。","- 选项D（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文只说甚至能创造 synthetic performers，Para.4 还有人类演员 Tori Thomas 参与拍摄，不能推出完全取代人类演员。","【命题技巧】","- 定位词改写：正确项将 tech-powered rival 与 no longer need...high walls 概括为 outside the old studio system。","- 限定词辨析：干扰项 B、D 分别用 solely 和 completely 将部分事实绝对化。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"The description of the Touch Grass shoot in Paragraph 5 is used to show that AI can _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"write dialogue and backstory for actors before filming begins"},{"key":"B","text":"combine a live performance with a generated backdrop while the scene is being shot"},{"key":"C","text":"delay post-production until directors have approved each location"},{"key":"D","text":"replace the director's monitor with a conventional sound stage"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·现场案例功能","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.5）：A small camera followed Thomas as she scrambled in a chase scene, then the AI superimposed her movement in real-time on to a field of swaying grass generated by a new Chinese AI model, Seedance 2.5...","- 原文（Para.5）：Whole scenes – actor and backdrop – were visible on the director’s handheld monitor as if they were filming in real locations.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。dialogue and backstory 出现在 Para.11 Dave Clark 的评论中，不是 Para.5 拍摄案例的功能。","- 选项B（正确）：案例显示摄影机追踪真人演员，AI 实时把她的动作叠加到生成的草地上，导演监视器能同时看到演员和背景。B 项准确概括这一功能。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文强调 real-time 和立即可见，不是延迟到后期制作。","- 选项D（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。原文说声音舞台只是办公室一角挂白床单，导演用手持监视器看合成画面，并不是用传统摄影棚替代监视器。","【命题技巧】","- 例证目的：Touch Grass 案例服务的是 AI 实时合成拍摄能力，不是电影剧情或演员表现。","- 跨段拼接排除：A 项使用后文词语制造熟悉感，但与第五段案例无关。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the spread of AI in film-making according to Paragraphs 6 and 7?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Netflix says AI was used in 300 of its 1,000 titles in 2026, and Pitt thinks it may help mid-budget films get made"},{"key":"B","text":"Netflix used AI in most of its 2026 titles, while Pitt opposes all AI tools in film production"},{"key":"C","text":"Imagine has replaced Ron Howard with an AI studio called Obsidian to direct The Code"},{"key":"D","text":"Kavan Cardoza predicts that major studios will necessarily lead the coming creative renaissance"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·正误判断","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 6-7","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：Promise is not alone in embracing the technology, which Netflix last week said it had used in 300 of its 1,000 titles in 2026.","- 原文（Para.7）：Brad Pitt this week said that...“AI is going to be the very thing that, if used as a tool, is going to help these mid-budget films...get made.”","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：Para.6 明确给出 Netflix 的比例是 1,000 部作品中的 300 部；Para.7 中 Brad Pitt 认为 AI 若作为工具使用，可帮助 4,000 万至 9,000 万美元的中等成本电影被拍出来。A 项两个信息点均正确。","- 选项B（错误）：数字与态度双重错误。300/1,000 是三成，不是 most；Pitt 也明确支持把 AI 当工具使用。","- 选项C（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。Obsidian 是 Imagine 旗下的 AI 工作室，The Code 仍是 Howard-directed animated feature，不是取代 Ron Howard。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Cardoza 预测的是 circumventing the studio giants，即绕开大型制片厂，不是由其主导。","【命题技巧】","- 比例换算：300 of 1,000 不能误读为 most，这是数字细节题的典型区分点。","- 人物归属：B、C、D 均把原文人物立场或项目关系反转或拼接。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The disagreement between Nolan and supporters of AI studios is most clearly about whether _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI models are technically capable of accelerating film production"},{"key":"B","text":"the film industry should reduce budgets for mid-budget films"},{"key":"C","text":"actors and writers have already lost all their jobs to AI"},{"key":"D","text":"AI-generated performers can become believable and publicly accepted parts of film-making"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】人物观点题·观点对比","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 3, 9, 10 and 11","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：Leading directors including Christopher Nolan and Guillermo del Toro have criticised generative technology, actors and writers are fearing for their jobs...","- 原文（Para.9）：“I’ve never seen a technology advancing so rapidly, so completely rejected by the public,” the director of The Odyssey has said.","- 原文（Para.11）：Dave Clark...said that with “great dialogue and backstory” AI-generated characters can become interesting and believable...Cardoza predicted “next year [AI actors will] be just as good as real actors”.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：答非所问陷阱。双方对 AI 发展速度和技术能力并不构成主要分歧；Nolan 也承认它 advancing so rapidly。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文没有说 Nolan 主张削减中等成本电影预算。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文说 actors and writers are fearing for their jobs，并没有说所有工作已经消失。","- 选项D（正确）：Nolan 强调公众强烈拒绝该技术，而 Clark 认为 AI 角色可以 believable，Cardoza 更预测 AI 演员明年会像真人演员一样好。分歧核心正是 AI 表演者的可信度与公众接受度。","【命题技巧】","- 观点对比：正确项必须把 Nolan 的 public rejection 与 Clark/Cardoza 的 believable/good as real actors 放在同一问题上对照。","- 共识与分歧区分：A 是双方可能都承认的技术事实，不能作为观点分歧点。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AI in Hollywood: Destruction or a New Golden Age?"},{"key":"B","text":"Synthetic Actors Have Already Ended Human Film-making"},{"key":"C","text":"Why Netflix and Disney Rejected Generative Technology"},{"key":"D","text":"From Singin' in the Rain to Seedance: A History of Special Effects"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：It is a controversial trend. Leading directors...have criticised generative technology, actors and writers are fearing for their jobs...","- 原文（Para.7）：He predicted a creative renaissance circumventing the studio giants...","- 原文（Para.11）：...hybrid AI films – human actors alongside AI technology – will prove 20% to 50% cheaper than conventional production.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：全文一方面呈现 AI 带来的降本、实时制作和创作复兴可能，另一方面呈现导演、演员和公众对失业、虚假表演与人类连接流失的担忧。A 项保留了 destruction 与 golden age 的核心张力。","- 选项B（错误）：过度推理陷阱。文中案例仍有人类演员参与，且 Promise 被描述为 hybrid AI films 的可能，不能说人类电影制作已经结束。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Netflix 已使用 AI，Google 和 Disney 也投资 Promise，标题中的 rejected 与原文相反。","- 选项D（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。片名和 Seedance 只是引入技术变迁的细节，文章不是特效史。","【命题技巧】","- 冲突型标题：文章围绕技术机会与行业恐惧展开，疑问式标题能同时覆盖两种立场。","- 时态控制：B 项的 Have Already Ended 将趋势绝对化为已完成事实。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.26检验题__完型填空.docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["From far more modest premises, they are making movies with rapidly accelerating AI models that create backgrounds, special effects and even “synthetic performers” – using US models but also driven by market-____【11】____ Chinese AI. Backed by Google, Silicon Valley venture capitalists and Disney, Promise is one of a ____【12】____ number of AI film studios in Hollywood.","It is a controversial ____【13】____. Leading directors including Christopher Nolan and Guillermo del Toro have ____【14】____ generative technology, actors and writers are ____【15】____ for their jobs, and the Democrat congresswoman Laura Friedman, who ____【16】____ Hollywood’s actors, writers and directors, ____【17】____: “We can’t wait until we see tens of thousands of American workers displaced.”","____【18】____ the excitement and energy about AI was ____【19】____ this week at Promise’s new base, when a human actor, Tori Thomas, waited for her call amid rows of computers on the studio’s AI-enabled horror film, Touch Grass, with a ____【20】____ in the low millions of dollars."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lagging"},{"key":"B","text":"leading"},{"key":"C","text":"failing"},{"key":"D","text":"emerging"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (leading)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·复合修饰","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第1句","【解析】","[A] lagging（落后的）：market-lagging 与“市场领先的中国 AI”方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] leading（领先的）：market-leading Chinese AI 是标准复合形容词，意为“市场领先的”。正确答案。","[C] failing（失败的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] emerging（新兴的）：语义可通，但不及 market-leading 精确。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shrinking"},{"key":"B","text":"falling"},{"key":"C","text":"forgotten"},{"key":"D","text":"rising"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (rising)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·语义方向","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] shrinking（缩小的）：与 a rising number 的扩张趋势相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] falling（下降的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] forgotten（被遗忘的）：语义不符。语义场干扰。","[D] rising（上升的）：one of a rising number 表示“越来越多中的一个”。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"policy"},{"key":"B","text":"investment"},{"key":"C","text":"trend"},{"key":"D","text":"accident"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (trend)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文概括","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] policy（政策）：后文是行业现象和公众争议，不是单一政策。语义场干扰。","[B] investment（投资）：前文有投资背景，但本段争议的是 AI 电影工作室这一趋势。近义干扰。","[C] trend（趋势）：It is a controversial trend 概括 AI 电影工作室增多这一现象。正确答案。","[D] accident（偶然事件）：语义不符。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"welcomed"},{"key":"B","text":"criticised"},{"key":"C","text":"ignored"},{"key":"D","text":"funded"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (criticised)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·态度语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] welcomed（欢迎）：与 controversial trend 和后文担忧相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] criticised（批评）：知名导演对生成式技术持批评态度。正确答案。","[C] ignored（忽视）：若忽视就不会公开表态。语义场干扰。","[D] funded（资助）：与导演批评语境不符。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hoping"},{"key":"B","text":"applying"},{"key":"C","text":"competing"},{"key":"D","text":"fearing"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (fearing)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·情感语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] hoping（希望）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] applying（申请）：可搭配 for，但不是工作岗位受威胁的核心语义。搭配干扰。","[C] competing（竞争）：行业竞争可通，但后文 displaced 说明是担忧失业。语义场干扰。","[D] fearing（担忧）：fearing for their jobs 意为“为工作担忧”。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"represents"},{"key":"B","text":"misleads"},{"key":"C","text":"criticises"},{"key":"D","text":"funds"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (represents)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·政治语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] represents（代表）：who represents Hollywood’s actors... 指该议员代表相关从业者。正确答案。","[B] misleads（误导）：与议员身份和语境不符。语义场干扰。","[C] criticises（批评）：她警告就业风险，但定语从句说明其代表关系。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] funds（资助）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"promised"},{"key":"B","text":"denied"},{"key":"C","text":"warned"},{"key":"D","text":"doubted"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (warned)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·引述动词","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] promised（承诺）：后文是风险警示而非正面承诺。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] denied（否认）：她没有否认风险，而是公开提示风险。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] warned（警告）：warned 后接警示性引语，提示美国工人可能被取代。正确答案。","[D] doubted（怀疑）：doubted 后应接怀疑内容，警示语气不足。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Because"},{"key":"B","text":"But"},{"key":"C","text":"And"},{"key":"D","text":"So"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (But)","analysis":["【题型】连词/逻辑衔接·转折","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] Because（因为）：前文批评与后文现场热情不是因果。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] But（但是）：前文争议与风险，后文现场兴奋形成转折。正确答案。","[C] And（并且）：前后不是同向递进。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] So（因此）：后文不是前文批评的结果。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"theoretical"},{"key":"B","text":"imaginary"},{"key":"C","text":"fading"},{"key":"D","text":"palpable"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (palpable)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·语境语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] theoretical（理论上的）：与 this week at Promise’s new base 的现场感相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] imaginary（想象中的）：现场热情真实存在。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] fading（消退的）：与 excitement and energy 的正向强度不符。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] palpable（明显的、几乎可触知的）：excitement was palpable 是常用搭配，表示热情显而易见。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"budget"},{"key":"B","text":"salary"},{"key":"C","text":"ticket"},{"key":"D","text":"script"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (budget)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·搭配语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第2句","【解析】","[A] budget（预算）：with a budget in the low millions of dollars 指“预算为几百万美元低位”。正确答案。","[B] salary（薪酬）：一部电影的 salary 语义不清且单复数不符。搭配干扰。","[C] ticket（票）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","[D] script（剧本）：剧本没有“low millions of dollars”的语境呼应。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.26 精读.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":689609,"date":"2026-08-26","range":"","title":"Will AI destroy film industry or usher in","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.26 精读.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.26 检验题__阅读理解.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":56184,"date":"2026-08-26","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.26 检验题__阅读理解.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.26检验题__完型填空.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":57680,"date":"2026-08-26","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.26检验题__完型填空.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"8.26杂志排版.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":764121,"date":"2026-08-26","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.26杂志排版.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
